EXT. ROOFTOP PIGEON COOP - SUNSET

A tar roof six stories up, patched with plywood. A wire-and-board coop sits against the stairwell. City below, orange and gold.

TAMSIN OKONKWO-REYES, 15, backpack, headphones around her neck, climbs through the roof hatch. She carries a thermos and a phone. She kneels beside the coop.

She opens the little door. A pigeon, grey and ruffled, hops onto her wrist.

She strokes it with one finger.

She sets the phone on the ledge. Taps the screen. A red dot blinks.

TAMSIN
Okay. Voice memo. Day twelve of the Great Return.

She pulls the pigeon close.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
Kevin hasn't flown home in six days. I don't think it's a navigation problem.

She hesitates. Then continues, quieter.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
I think he likes it wherever he's going.

She stops the recording. Plays it back.

TAMSIN (V.O.)
(phone)
I think he likes it wherever he's going.

She frowns. Taps again. Plays the previous bit.

TAMSIN (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(phone)
Kevin hasn't flown home in six days.

She sets down the phone. She watches the sun slide behind the water towers. She lifts her wrist. The pigeon hops off, fluttering up onto the lip of the coop.

TAMSIN
Go, then.

He doesn't. He tucks his beak under his wing.

She laughs, wipes her eyes with her sleeve, and sits on the warm tar with her back against the coop.

She presses record again.

TAMSIN (CONT'D)
(to the phone)
Day thirteen. He stayed.
